rcbroo9@aol.com (Rcbroo9) writes:
> I have read the FAQ on recovering a game and everything, but I still haven't
> been able to recover my game that just crashed.  Does anyone have any other
> more detailed instructions that could help me out? Thanks.

What OS are you playing on? What version of NetHack? What were the
circumstances of the crash, and was anything written to the paniclog
file?  What files were created in the NetHack playground that look
related (name or timestamp) to the crashed game? What have you tried
already, and in what way did it fail?

(Some ports of NetHack have the recover program kick in automatically;
some don't and need it to be run manually, the details of doing so
differing slightly between them. Without more information, there's no
detailed advice that can be given.)

